# The Quiet Archive - EP09 A Quiet Night in Edo Japan (an autumn night in the early 1800s, late Edo period)
# Structure: the night is told by the temple time-bells (sunset bell -> fourth bell -> deep night), a first for the channel.
# New scenes: "nihonbashi" = the arched wooden Nihonbashi bridge from the riverbank at dusk: railings with bronze-capped
#   posts, people crossing with paper lanterns, moored cargo boats, white-walled storehouses on the far bank, the castle
#   keep in silhouette and Mount Fuji pale against the afterglow; the river carries the lamplight (_wlights).
# "sumida" = the wide Sumida river by moonlight: a roofed pleasure boat (yakatabune) with lit paper walls and a boatman
#   poling at the stern drifts across once per loop (_yakata), a long low bridge on many piers in the distance, a weeping
#   willow on the near bank with swaying strands (_willow) and a little soba stall with its lantern and wind chime.
# "lanes" = a merchant lane of two-storey wooden shophouses: dark tiled roofs, latticed fronts glowing from inside,
#   shop curtains (noren), round paper lanterns (chochin) hanging from the eaves that swing gently (_chochin), a ward gate
#   with a wicket door, a fire-watch ladder tower with its bell, a bathhouse chimney breathing steam (smoke).
# "pagoda" = the five-storey pagoda at Asakusa: five sweeping roofs with upturned eaves and a bronze finial (_pagoda),
#   stone lanterns (toro) with lit windows, a bell in its open belfry, a maple and pampas grass in the foreground.
# "tatami" = inside a row-house room: paper sliding screens (shoji) with a moonlit pine shadow, tatami edges in
#   perspective, a paper floor lamp (andon) with its soft glow, a brazier with a kettle breathing steam (_steam), a tiny
#   bamboo insect cage, folded bedding, a vase of pampas grass.
# New "leaves" particles (small autumn maple leaves turning as they fall); palette keys "lacquer" and "washi".
